# Tutorials: each story is one page that walks through a game, step by step. The rules that no
# story shows (the computer commander, a draw) are tested on their own.

Story: Taking a tower from Red
  As a commander of a team
  I want to see how my drones take a tower
  So that I send enough drones, and not too many

  Red holds the west tower. You send one drone to circle it, and you watch the control bar of the
  tower. Red keeps the tower until the bar gets back to the middle. Then a Red drone comes to
  fight, and the bar stops.

  Scenario: One drone against the west tower
    Given the west tower is held by Red
    And the control of the west tower is -100 %
    When the Blue drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is -50 %
    And the west tower is held by Red
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the west tower is neutral
    And the control of the west tower is 0 %
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    When the Red drones in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 50 %
    And the circle of the west tower is contested

Story: Sending enough drones
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know how many drones a tower needs
  So that I take it fast

  A drone must fly in the circle of a tower to count. You land a drone next to the west tower,
  and nothing happens. Then you send two drones to circle it, and they take it in 10 s: half the
  time of one drone.

  Scenario: A landed drone, then two drones in the air
    When the Blue drones on the ground in the west circle are 1
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the control of the west tower is 0 %
    When the Blue drones in the west circle are 2
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the west tower is held by Blue

Story: Winning a game
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know how a game ends
  So that I know when to hold and when to attack

  Each tower that your team holds gives one point each second. You take a second tower, and your
  score goes up twice as fast. At 500 points, your team wins, and the game stops.

  Scenario: Two towers, then 500 points
    When the towers held by Blue are 2
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the score of Blue is 20 points
    When the score of Blue is 495 points
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the game of Towers is won by Blue
    And the score of Blue is 500 points
    When the game runs for 1 minute
    Then the game of Towers is won by Blue
    And the score of Blue is 500 points

Story: Scouting in the fog
  As a commander of a team
  I want to know what my map shows me
  So that I do not trust what I cannot see

  A Red scout flies near one of your drones, and your map shows it. It flies away into the fog,
  and your map keeps it where you last saw it. Then Red takes the east tower in the fog. Your
  map does not show it until a drone of yours looks again.

  Scenario: The scout, then the east tower
    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen
    When the Red scout flies into the fog for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is last seen
    And the age of the Red scout on the Blue map is 10 s
    When the Red drones in the east circle are 1
    When the game runs for 20 seconds
    Then the east tower is held by Red
    And the east tower on the Blue map is neutral
    When a Blue drone flies near the east tower
    Then the east tower on the Blue map is held by Red
